---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../components/Byline.astro";
import DualDoors from "../components/DualDoors.astro";
import LegalNote from "../components/LegalNote.astro";
import IndexSeriesTable from "../components/IndexSeriesTable.astro";
import { LINKS, CANON_PATHS, linkClass, ext } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const path = "/retailbi-firearm-sales-index";
const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "How to read the Index", path },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How the Index is built — and how to read it | FFL Intel"
  description="Gearfire’s monthly Firearm Sales Index is a register series. Same stores. New firearms. Subject to revision. That is a real thing. It is still last month."
  path={path}
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.copilot}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3">
      The Index
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white text-balance mb-4">
      How the Index is built — and how to read it
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 mb-6">
      Same stores. New firearms. A percent versus last year. Subject to
      revision. That is a grown-up series. It is not the whole market.
    </p>
    <Byline dateLabel="August 13, 2026" read="6 min" />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.copilot)}
        alt="Betsy — demand research"
        width="1792"
        height="1008"
        class="w-full object-cover object-top max-h-80"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif">
      <p>
        Gearfire put the Index on Outdoor Wire on 3 September 2025. First
        print scheduled the fifth. Method, from the April 2026 file and every
        file like it: pull POS and ecommerce from the network, keep new
        firearms, keep only retailers who reported in both this window and
        last year’s, print the percent change. Openings and closings do not
        pose as demand. Used guns do not pose as new.
      </p>
      <p>
        Seymour, at launch: the supply chain “deserves a measurement that
        isn’t clouded by irrelevant information, circumstantial influences,
        and unfounded assumptions.” He was talking about NICS. He was not
        talking about search. Those are different clouds.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8">
      <p
        class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-sky-400 mb-3"
      >
        The public series
      </p>
      <IndexSeriesTable />
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif">
      <p>
        Read it as a year, not a slide. August opened ugly. November was
        uglier. The December file printed the 2025 year at minus 12.1. The
        annual called the climate about 13 percent. January’s first print was
        minus 6.2; February’s file moved it to minus 5.7. March printed minus
        11.9, year-to-date minus 8.2. Their 2026 outlook, on the NSSF note,
        was another seven to twelve percent down. March is how an outlook
        starts to look like a year.
      </p>
      <p>
        As of 13 August 2026 Outdoor Wire’s last monthly is still the April 13
        file. Samples move. Believe the revision line. A same-store new-gun
        print is the register talking about last month. It is not NICS. It is
        not the used-gun aisle. It is not the sentence on a dealer site at
        9:40 p.m. Definition:{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.fortress} class={linkClass} {...ext}>RetailBI vs Betsy</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href={LINKS.gseIndex} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GSE Index spoke</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <DualDoors />
    <p class="mt-10"><LegalNote fortress /></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
